  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-f723b631-7fff-0642-5835-e5f5cfcab3cb&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;By reason of a lack of an affordable housing financial contribution, would, therefore, fail to adequately contribute towards the provision of mixed and balanced communities and housing needs in the local area. The development would, therefore, conflict with Policy LP13 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;I&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;n the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 Agreement securing appropriate mitigation by restricting future occupiers of the development from obtaining parking permits within the CPZ, the development would likely exacerbate existing parking stress and congestion on the surrounding highway network. The development would, therefore, be contrary to Policy LP45 of the LP33 and Policy T6 of the London Plan (2021). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-0be16771-7fff-d9ff-5336-05409bb6e4e4&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement securing the financial contribution towards carbon off-setting having been submitted or completed, the proposal would fail to secure sufficient energy efficiency measures and/or financial contribution towards carbon offsetting and would, therefore, result in an unacceptable level of carbon dioxide emissions, contrary to Policy LP55 of the LP33.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
